        "original_id": "0ca57723-0cdb-5ea9-a0ff-fef3a3542500",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: J. Eric Holmes, Gary Gygax, Dave Arneson\n- Products: Dungeons & Dragons Basic Set\n- Organizations: University of Southern California School of Medicine\n- Topics: fantasy role-playing games, Edgar Rice Burroughs\n\nFacts:\n- J. Eric Holmes wrote the first edition of the Dungeons & Dragons Basic Set based on the original work of Gary Gygax and Dave Arneson.\n- John Eric Holmes M.D. was born on February 16, 1930.\n- John Eric Holmes was an associate professor of neurology at the University of Southern California School of Medicine.\n- John Eric Holmes was an author and promoter of fantasy role-playing games.\n- John Eric Holmes was a noted fan and enthusiast of Edgar Rice Burroughs.\n- John Eric Holmes was an American writer of non-fiction, fantasy, and science fiction.\n- John Eric Holmes died on March 20, 2010.",
